A||N||4||Kelvin Vivian||Pegging Temp Needle||||1||
Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||01-28-2001||08:39 AM||||Is there a way, other than lightly banging the top of the instrument pod, to get the temperature needle to read correctly.<P>Usually when I fire up the 88 GT, the temp needle pegs and remains hidden (reading a temperature off the scales)... <P>Kelvin Vivian<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/Cove/2449/finalfront.jpg">  1987 SE - 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-28-2001||09:48 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A> <P>Go to the link above and it'll never peg while starting again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||CJ||01-28-2001||10:19 AM||||Instead of getting into a wiring project on my 88 GT, I took the cluster out and glued a piece of black foam tape above the top end of the scale.  When the needle swings full hot when starting, the foam stops it from getting jammed up there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-28-2001||11:00 AM||||The only problem with a needle stop is that sometimes the needle loosenes itself off the spindle then the needle reads the wrong temp or the needle falls off. The needle is just glued onto the spindle.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||01-28-2001||11:20 AM||||What wiring project.... <P>you need to drop the steering column so you can get to the ignition switch.<P>unplug the switch.<P>use a paper clip to release the terminal to the gauge from the plug. (There is a small notch next to the terminals. the paper clip goes there.)<P>plug it back in and bolt up the column. <P>Whole thing takes 20 minutes max. I did mine in the park durring lunch one day....||||reg||1
